    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only runnable test class, and the full `mvn test` build is green.\n\nThe change is complete. Summary of what I implemented:\n\n**Rule:** Creating an owner is now rejected with **409 Conflict** when another owner already has the same `lastName` **and** the same `address` \u2014 compared case-insensitively after trimming and collapsing internal whitespace runs to a single space \u2014 **unless** the request sets `sharesHousehold: true`.\n\n**Changes (standard Spring/OpenAPI-first idioms):**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a write-only boolean `sharesHousehold` property to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` exposes the flag (Jackson was already ignoring it as an unknown field, silently dropping the opt-in).\n\n2. **`rest/advice/DuplicateOwnerException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` mirroring the existing `DuplicateTelephoneException` pattern.\n\n3. **`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 a new `@ExceptionHandler` mapping `DuplicateOwnerException` to a `409` `ProblemDetail`, reporting `lastName` and `address` in the `errors` array.\n\n4. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `requireUniqueHousehold(...)` (invoked from the existing `normalizeAndValidate` create path) plus a `collapseWhitespace` helper. It short-circuits when `sharesHousehold` is true, otherwise scans existing owners and throws when a case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed `lastName`+`address` match is found.\n\n5. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 ignored the write-only `sharesHousehold` on the `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` response mapping.\n\nAll three acceptance tests (`coreRejectsSameLastNameAndAddress`, `functionalityAllowsDifferentAddress`, `functionalityAllowsWithSharesHousehold`) and the full `mvn test` build are green.",
