    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`, as the code currently stands. The endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:109`).\n\n## Validations (in order)\n\n1. **Authentication** \u2014 HTTP Basic auth via the Spring Security filter chain (only when `petclinic.security.enable=true`).\n2. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires the `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` authority; otherwise \u2192 403.\n3. **Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto`** (`@Valid @RequestBody`, runs before the method body) \u2192 400 on failure:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n   - `registrationDate`: `@Valid` only (optional)\n   - `sharesHousehold`: no constraints\n4. **Required-fields check** (`validateRequiredFields`) \u2014 re-checks `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` for null/blank (catches whitespace-only values that passed `@Size`) \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n5. **Telephone normalization** (`telephoneNormalizer.normalize`) \u2014 converts to canonical E.164 (default `+61`, 8\u201315 digits); invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n6. **Unique telephone** \u2014 loads all owners, canonicalizes each existing phone, rejects a match \u2192 `DuplicateTelephoneException` (409).\n7. **Unique household** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold == true`, collapses whitespace on `lastName`+`address`, loads all owners, rejects a case-insensitive match on both \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException` (409).\n8. **Entity-level constraints at flush** \u2014 the `Owner` entity carries `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern` (E.164)/`@Email` constraints that Hibernate may validate on persist.\n\n## Side-effects (in order)\n\n1. **Mutates the incoming DTO**: writes the normalized telephone back onto the DTO.\n2. **Normalizes email**: lower-cases it (null/blank left untouched).\n3. **Defaults `registrationDate`**: if null, sets it to `LocalDate.now()`.\n4. **Maps** DTO \u2192 `Owner` (MapStruct); id/customerCode/pets not set here.\n5. **Generates and sets `customerCode`**: `<first-3-letters-of-lastName-uppercased>-<NNNN>`, where the sequence number = current owner count + 1 (another full owner load).\n6. **Persists**: `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `@Transactional` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` (plain Spring Data JPA save; no lifecycle callbacks).\n7. **Builds response**: maps the saved entity back to `OwnerDto` (deriving `displayName` and `initials`), sets the `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, returns **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notably absent\n\nNo `@PrePersist`/`@PreUpdate` or entity lifecycle callbacks, no `@EventListener`/`@TransactionalEventListener`, no password encoding (owners have no password), no email/notification sending, and no audit logging exist anywhere in this path.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the two uniqueness checks plus the customer-code generation each call `findAllOwners()`, so a single create loads the full owners table three times \u2014 and the uniqueness checks are read-then-write without a DB unique constraint, so they're subject to races under concurrency."
